Photos reach the widgets again. The app prepared a picture and waited for it forever: preparation stalled on the very first step, while texts went to the home screen ahead of images. That is why it looked as if only the status changed and the photo stayed the same, no matter how often you replaced it.

The photo grid fills itself. Partner's shots used to arrive only if you opened the widgets tab in the app; those who never did saw empty cells.

No step of preparing a picture waits without a limit any more. Network, codec, disk — each has its own budget; if a shot does not make it, the previous one stays and the next pass tries again.

Cycle is unlocked by the subscription, not by gender. The card used to appear only for a female profile, so anyone who had not picked a gender never found it. Cycle also no longer sends to the store those who already paid: the app waits for the purchase answer first.

Widgets on iPhone got lighter: avatars are no longer decoded at full size and stop eating the memory an extension barely has.
